  "arrangerNotes": "2/4 time (eighth = 0.5 beat). Verified against the LilyPond score on Japanese Wikipedia (same engraving on Chinese Wikipedia). D drum: exactly as the score, which dips to low 3 and low 4 on 'Doodle dandy', so D minLayout 15. C drum: the C drum has no low 3 or 4, so the 'Yankee Doodle, keep it up, Yankee Doodle dandy' phrase (2 lines) is played one octave higher. All other notes are as written. C minLayout 11. Medium because of the dotted rhythms and the low register. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
  "verified": true
